`undici` looks like it was previously only coming in transitively via `jsdom`, so adding it to top-level `dependencies` promotes a test-only package into the production install set and also introduces its Node engine requirement at runtime. If the goal is just to pin a patched transitive version, could you move this to `overrides` in `package.json` instead of `dependencies` and regenerate `package-lock.json`?

Something like this should be enough:

```json
{
  "overrides": {
    "keyv": "5.1.0",
    "minimatch": ">=10.2.1",
    "undici": "^7.24.5"
  }
}
